From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kant <283011337+muradkant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:55:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Wait for events instead of polling

The capture thread checked for a free buffer every 0.5 ms and the
encoder thread for a captured frame every 1 ms: two thousand wakeups a
second whatever the frame rate, keeping a core out of its idle states
for the whole recording. Block on a condition variable instead.

The capture thread now waits on the compositor and an eventfd together,
so a stop request (signal, write failure, lost audio) ends the recording
at once even while no frame is coming, as happens with damage tracking
on an unchanging output.
